From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:39:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scheme: a SIGKILLed caller still cancels its pending request
 (issue #401)

When a thread blocked in a scheme call is SIGKILLed, for example the
other threads of an exiting process, UserInner::call returned EINTR
without sending a cancellation. The scheme kept the request, and ptyd
handed the next line typed to the dead reader: after nc exits in a
devsh session, the next command line is lost. Send the Cancel first,
then return EINTR.
---
 src/scheme/user.rs | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/scheme/user.rs b/src/scheme/user.rs
index d91ae0ab..1f686154 100644
--- a/src/scheme/user.rs
+++ b/src/scheme/user.rs
@@ -336,7 +336,11 @@ impl UserInner {
                                 callee_responsible,
                             };
 
-                            maybe_eintr?;
+                            // A caller that is being SIGKILLed (for example a
+                            // thread of an exiting process) still cancels the
+                            // request, so the scheme drops it. Otherwise ptyd
+                            // hands the next line typed to the dead reader and
+                            // it is lost (issue #401).
 
                             // We do not want to preempt between sending the
                             // cancellation and blocking again where we might
@@ -360,6 +364,8 @@ impl UserInner {
                                 token.token(),
                             );
 
+                            maybe_eintr?;
+
                             // 1. If cancellation was requested and arrived
                             // before the scheme processed the request, an
                             // acknowledgement will be sent back after the
